The synonym "proline" is related to "L-proline" but not identical. "Proline" can refer to both L-proline and D-proline, which are stereoisomers. In biomedical contexts, specifying "L-proline" is crucial because L-proline is the biologically active form involved in protein synthesis and collagen production, while D-proline is not typically found in proteins. Therefore, while they are related, they are not interchangeable without potential loss of specificity.
