The "submandibular ganglion" is specifically associated with the lingual nerve and provides postsynaptic fibers to the submandibular and sublingual glands. In contrast, the "maxillary ganglion" is associated with the maxillary nerve and provides postsynaptic fibers to the lacrimal gland, nasal mucosa, and palatine glands. These are distinct anatomical entities with different functions and locations, thus they are semantically different.
